export const CONCIERGE_DASHBOARD_KNOWLEDGE = "# ChainMore Dashboard Knowledge\n\nSurface: signed-in merchants only.\n\nHow the merchant dashboard at `app.chainmore.io` works today. Use it to\nanswer \"how do I …\" and \"where do I find …\" questions. Describe only what is\nwritten here. If a feature is not listed, say it is not in the dashboard and\npoint to `support@chainmore.io`. Never promise a feature, a date or a change.\n\nThe signed-in person's role and the mode their dashboard shows come with each\nquestion. A page or button that their role does not have: say so plainly and\nname who can do it (usually the account owner or an admin). Do not walk them\nthrough steps they cannot take.\n\n## Navigation\n\nThe left menu, in English and German. Pages a role cannot open are hidden.\n\n| Page (EN / DE) | Roles that see it |\n|---|---|\n| Overview / Übersicht | all |\n| Status / Status | all |\n| Notifications / Benachrichtigungen | all |\n| Onboarding / Onboarding | owner, admin, developer, support |\n| Payments / Zahlungen | all |\n| Customers / Kunden | owner, admin, finance, support, viewer |\n| Payment lookup / Zahlung suchen | all |\n| Sessions / Sessions | all |\n| API keys / API-Keys | owner, admin, developer |\n| Payout targets / Auszahlungsziele | owner, admin, finance |\n| Webhooks / Webhooks | owner, admin, developer |\n| Deliveries / Auslieferungen | owner, admin, developer, support |\n| Team / Team | owner, admin, support |\n| Billing / Abrechnung | owner, admin, finance, viewer |\n| Audit log / Audit-Log | all |\n| Integration / Integration | owner, admin, developer |\n| Settings / Einstellungen | owner, admin |\n\nRoles: owner, admin, developer, finance, support, viewer. Someone who opens a\npage their role cannot use sees \"This page is not available for your role\".\n\n## First sign-in\n\n- After ChainMore approves a registration, the person named in it gets an\n  e-mail from ChainMore. Its button opens a page to confirm the e-mail\n  address and choose a password. The link works for at most 72 hours and is\n  personal; do not forward it.\n- Then sign in at `app.chainmore.io` with \"Sign in\" / \"Anmelden\".\n- Before the dashboard opens, a page \"Review your account documents\" /\n  \"Kontodokumente prüfen\" lists the documents with their \"Document version\".\n  Each document opens inline; \"Open …\" shows it on its own page.\n- Every person confirms three acknowledgements for themselves: the test\n  environment notice, the terms for their own use, and the confidentiality\n  obligations. Then \"Save acknowledgements\" / \"Bestätigungen speichern\".\n- An owner or admin also accepts the company terms, with the box \"I am\n  authorised to represent the company and accept these company terms.\" Only\n  an owner or admin can do this, and it is needed once per document version\n  for the whole account. They can save their own acknowledgements first and\n  accept the company terms later.\n- Until an owner or admin has accepted the company terms, every other team\n  member sees \"The company terms still need to be accepted by an account\n  owner or administrator.\" and the dashboard stays closed for them.\n- When ChainMore publishes a new document version, everyone sees the page\n  again and confirms the new version.\n- The ChainMore Concierge opens only after this page is done.\n- The page also says that stablecoin payments can move real funds even in\n  test mode.\n\n## Test and live mode\n\n- Three separate steps. When ChainMore approves a registration, the account\n  starts in test mode. Setting up the login (confirm the e-mail address,\n  choose a password, sign in) does not change the mode. Live access is a\n  separate decision: ChainMore switches it on after reviewing the business\n  profile. It cannot be switched on in the dashboard.\n- The bar below the top bar shows the mode on every page, with a \"Dashboard\n  mode\" / \"Dashboard-Modus\" selector. It lists only the modes the account\n  may use: \"Test mode\" / \"Testmodus\" before live access, \"Test mode\" and\n  \"Live mode\" / \"Live-Modus\" after it. Each team member picks their own\n  mode; the choice is saved for their login, not in the browser.\n- Once live access is on, the dashboard opens in live mode unless the person\n  picked test mode before. Test data stays separate and shows again in test\n  mode. If ChainMore switches live access off, the dashboard goes back to\n  test mode.\n- \"Refresh mode\" / \"Modus aktualisieren\" reloads the mode. If the mode\n  changed in another tab or on ChainMore's side, the dashboard does not carry\n  out the request and says so. Check the mode shown and repeat the action if\n  it is still wanted.\n- Test mode: wallet payments still move real money on the real networks, and\n  real network fees apply. Do not send a wallet payment in test mode before\n  the payment route and the test amount have been agreed with ChainMore\n  (`support@chainmore.io`).\n- Payments, sessions, API keys, webhooks, deliveries, payout targets,\n  exports, notification settings and the business profile are separate per\n  mode. Team and audit log are shared.\n\n## Using the dashboard\n\nHow each page works. Page names are given in English and German. Which pages\na person sees depends on their role; a page their role cannot open is not\nin the menu.\n\nFor every action: if it fails twice, stop and email `support@chainmore.io`\nwith the Error ID, payment ID or merchant ID. Never send API keys, signing\nsecrets or passwords.\n\n### Overview / Übersicht\n\nEveryone. The account at a glance for the mode shown.\n\n- \"Integration status\": merchant, default currency, active API keys, webhook\n  endpoints and the last delivery, with \"Open keys\" and \"Open webhooks\".\n- \"Ready for your first payment\": server API key, webhook endpoint, first\n  event received. \"Fix next item\" opens the next missing step; when all are\n  ready, \"Open integration guide\". It shows readiness for a first checkout,\n  not whether a payment goes all the way to payout.\n- \"Setup progress\": business profile, test API key, webhook endpoint, webhook\n  test event, first test payment, live access and live API key, with \"Next\n  step\". The live access line shows what ChainMore decided: business profile\n  needed, test mode, more information needed, approved or not approved.\n- \"Webhook delivery\": deliveries of the last 24 hours, with \"Open\n  deliveries\". It says nothing about the payments themselves.\n- \"Payments at a glance\": counts by status and requested amounts. Requested\n  is not settled.\n- \"Needs attention\": delayed, under review, failed and expired payments. The\n  buttons open the matching list, for example \"Open review queue\". A failed\n  or expired payment alone does not decide whether the order is paid: when\n  the checkout link also has an `intent_id`, the payment can continue on that\n  payment intent, and a completed intent is paid even though the first\n  payment reads expired. Check the link and, if it has one, the intent before\n  treating the order as unpaid. If the customer says money left their wallet,\n  email support with the payment ID.\n- \"Settled amounts\" and \"Payment routes\": booked totals for a period, with\n  \"Open payment lookup\".\n- \"Recent activity\": the last 5 payments and checkout sessions.\n\n### Status\n\nEveryone. The open items of this account, not ChainMore's system status.\n\n- The top shows \"Nothing to do\", \"Attention needed\" or \"Action needed\".\n- Signals: \"Payments to review\", \"Webhook deliveries\" and \"Route notes\".\n- \"Next action\" links to the fix, for example \"Review payments\" or \"Check\n  webhook delivery failures\".\n- \"Status data could not load\": reload the page; if it stays, email support.\n\n### Notifications / Benachrichtigungen\n\nEveryone can look; owners and admins save.\n\n- Choose which alerts count in the dashboard: \"Payment problems\", \"Failed\n  webhook deliveries\" and \"Account review and live access\", and the\n  \"Minimum level\": also alerts to keep an eye on, or only alerts with a clear\n  next step. Then \"Save settings\" / \"Einstellungen speichern\".\n- Result: \"Settings saved\". The settings apply to the mode the dashboard\n  shows.\n- Alerts appear only in the dashboard. They are not sent by e-mail, Slack or\n  pager.\n\n### Onboarding\n\nOwners, admins, developers and support.\n\n- \"Setup steps\": connect (test key, webhook endpoint, test event), test\n  payment, go live. \"For your developers\" links the pages they need.\n- \"Live access status\": what ChainMore decided. There is no switch for it in\n  the dashboard. \"Live access approved\" means a live key can be created once\n  the person picks live mode.\n- \"Business profile\" (owners and admins submit): Website, Contact email,\n  Country, Business type, Expected monthly volume and \"What you'll use\n  payments for\", then \"Submit profile\" / \"Profil einreichen\". Result:\n  \"Profile submitted. ChainMore can now review your account.\" This starts\n  ChainMore's review. Later, use \"Update profile\" only when something\n  changed.\n- If the profile cannot be submitted, try again later; if it fails twice,\n  email support.\n\n### Payments / Zahlungen\n\nEveryone.\n\n- Newest first, 50 per page, \"Load more\". Columns: order or payment ID,\n  amount, status, mode, checkout, created, updated.\n- Find a payment: enter the exact `merchant_order_id` or payment ID in\n  \"Reference\" / \"Referenz\", optionally a status and \"Created from\" /\n  \"Created to\" (UTC days), then \"Apply filters\" / \"Filter anwenden\". The\n  search needs the exact value; it does not find parts of a reference,\n  amounts, wallets or names.\n- Click a row for the details: IDs, status, mode, requested amount, the asset\n  it settles in, times, transaction hashes of on-chain steps, and a timeline\n  from \"Payment created\" to \"Settlement recorded\" with \"Open evidence\".\n  \"Search this payment\" opens it in Payment lookup.\n- Under review: payments that did not go through on their own and are checked\n  by hand, reached from Overview or Status (\"Open review queue\"). There is\n  nothing to do there except open the payment; if one stays stuck, email\n  support with the payment ID.\n- Refunds and cancellations are not possible in the dashboard. Contact\n  `support@chainmore.io` with the payment ID.\n- Exports (owners, admins, developers, finance):\n  - \"Export CSV\" / \"CSV exportieren\" downloads the filtered list, up to 5,000\n    rows. Columns: `payment_id`, `merchant_order_id`, `environment`,\n    `requested_amount_minor`, `requested_currency`, `canonical_asset`,\n    `public_status`, `checkout_required`, `mode`, `created_at`,\n    `updated_at`.\n  - The export holds requested amounts and status only: no fees, no net\n    amount, no settled amount and no transaction hashes. For fees and net per\n    period, use Billing or \"Settled totals\" on Payment lookup.\n  - \"Large exports\": set both \"Created from\" and \"Created to\" (at most 32\n    days), then \"Request CSV\" or \"Request JSONL\"; \"Download\" once it is\n    ready. If one stays \"Being prepared\" for more than 30 minutes, use\n    \"Export CSV\" in smaller date ranges and tell support.\n  - An export is only a file. It triggers nothing, not even a refund. There\n    are no invoices, tax documents, settlement or payout exports.\n\n### Customers / Kunden\n\nOwners, admins, finance, support and viewers.\n\n- Enter the exact `customer_reference` your integration sent, then \"Open\n  customer activity\" / \"Kundenaktivität öffnen\". It shows that customer's\n  payments and totals.\n- It is not a general customer search: there is no search by name, e-mail or\n  wallet. Otherwise use \"Open payment lookup\".\n\n### Payment lookup / Zahlung suchen\n\nEveryone.\n\n- Search by `merchant_order_id`, `customer_reference` or payment ID, exact\n  match, then \"Search\" / \"Suchen\". The result shows the route, the amounts at\n  each step and \"Payment evidence\" with \"Payment steps\" and block explorer\n  links.\n- \"Settled totals\": \"Created from\" / \"Created to\", at most 32 days (default\n  the last 30), then \"Apply\". Shows payments, settled, gross USDC, your net,\n  fees, exceptions and the on-chain check.\n- \"Payment routes at a glance\": payments and settlements per route for the\n  period. The individual evidence is what counts.\n\n### Sessions\n\nEveryone. The customers' checkout sessions, not login sessions.\n\n- \"Search loaded sessions\" and \"State\" filter the rows already loaded; use\n  \"Load more\" before concluding a session is missing.\n- Click a session for \"Customer status\" and \"Your next step\". \"Show technical\n  session details\" adds the technical state and a failure code, if any.\n\n### API keys / API-Keys\n\nOwners, admins and developers.\n\n- Create: \"Create key\" / \"Key erstellen\", give it a name. \"Key mode\" shows\n  the mode the dashboard shows; the key gets that mode. \"Create\", then copy\n  the key and press \"I've saved it\". The key is shown only once. Test keys\n  start with `cm_test_`, live keys with `cm_live_`; live keys need live\n  access.\n- \"Rotate\" makes a new key and switches the old one off in the same step.\n  The new key is shown only after the rotation, so requests with the old key\n  fail from that moment until the server uses the new one. Have the server\n  change ready, rotate, copy the new key, put it on the server at once and\n  check that calls work.\n- Without a gap: \"Create key\" for a second key, put it on the server, check\n  that calls work, then \"Revoke\" the old key. Several keys can be active at\n  the same time.\n- \"Revoke\" switches a key off for good. Anything still using it fails right\n  away.\n- The list shows name, prefix, status, mode and created date. It does not\n  show when a key was last used.\n- A lost key cannot be shown again. Create or rotate a key instead.\n\n### Payout targets / Auszahlungsziele\n\nOwners and admins change targets; finance can view them.\n\n- Where your money arrives. Without a target the checkout offers no payment\n  method.\n- \"Add target\": enter the receiving address. ChainMore suggests token and\n  network (a TRON address means USDT on Tron, a plain 0x address USDT on\n  Arbitrum). Networks: Ethereum, Arbitrum, Polygon, Optimism, BNB Smart Chain,\n  Base, Tron. Tokens: USDT and USDC. Then \"Confirm target\".\n- Check the address twice. A payout to a wrong address cannot be recovered.\n- \"Edit\" changes only the priority: 0 to 1000, default 100, lower wins among\n  targets of the same token. To use a new address for the same token and\n  network, add the target again; the new address replaces the old one for new\n  payments.\n- \"Disable\" stops a target for new payments; it stays listed and\n  \"Reactivate\" turns it on again. Payments already created keep their\n  address.\n- Declared USDC targets can be used by the Core USDC payment path when that\n  path is enabled on the running release. A checkout link with its own\n  `usdc` destination names that explicit target; whether it binds a Core\n  payment or a USDC/CCTP intent depends on the enabled route. Saving a\n  target alone does not activate a payment route. For each link, offer USDC\n  only when `usdc` appears in `available_payment_methods`; do not infer\n  current availability from the target list or from code on Main.\n- Everyone else sees \"Only an owner or admin can change payout targets.\"\n\n### Webhooks\n\nOwners, admins and developers.\n\n- \"Add endpoint\" / \"Endpoint hinzufügen\": a public HTTPS URL; events as a\n  comma-separated list, empty means all events. \"Create\". The signing secret\n  `whsec_…` is shown once.\n- \"Edit\" changes URL, events and the \"Active\" switch, then \"Save\". Endpoints\n  cannot be deleted; switch them off instead.\n- \"Rotate secret\": the new secret is shown once. For 14 days each delivery\n  also carries a signature with the old secret in\n  `X-ChainMore-Signature-Previous`. A banner reminds you after 90 days.\n- \"Send test event\" sends a signed test event with `\"test_event\": true`. It\n  needs an active endpoint.\n\n### Deliveries / Auslieferungen\n\nOwners, admins, developers and support.\n\n- Every delivery with status, attempts, last error and time. \"Search\" finds\n  a payment, event, endpoint, status code or error; \"Load more\" loads older\n  ones.\n- \"Replay\" / \"Erneut senden\" sends the same event again with a new\n  `event_id`, signed with the current secret. Owners, admins and developers\n  can replay; support can only look. Test events cannot be replayed; send a\n  new test event instead.\n- Before a replay, check that your server handles the same order only once.\n\n### Team / Team-Zugriff\n\nOwners and admins manage; support can view.\n\n1. \"Invite a teammate\": enter the e-mail and a role (admin, developer,\n   finance, support or viewer), then \"Create invitation\". Owners cannot be\n   invited.\n2. No e-mail is sent. Tell the person yourself.\n3. The person signs in at `app.chainmore.io` with exactly that e-mail address.\n   They need a ChainMore login first; if they do not have one, email\n   `support@chainmore.io` with their address. On their first sign-in they\n   join with the invited role.\n4. An invitation expires after 14 days. An expired invitation cannot be\n   renewed in the dashboard; contact support.\n5. One person can belong to only one merchant account.\n\n- Change a role: pick it in the member's row, \"Save role\". You cannot change\n  your own role or an owner's.\n- Remove someone: \"Remove access\", then confirm. Owners cannot be removed;\n  ownership cannot be transferred in the dashboard.\n- \"Revoke\" withdraws a pending invitation.\n\n### Billing / Abrechnung\n\nOwners, admins, finance and viewers.\n\n- \"Created from\" / \"Created to\" (at most 32 days), then \"Apply\". Shows\n  settled totals and ChainMore fees for that period. It is an overview, not\n  an invoice.\n- Some payment types have no USDC value there, so \"Your net\" can read \"Not\n  available\".\n- \"Reconciliation\" compares booked totals with on-chain records and names\n  the next step if they differ.\n\n### Audit log / Audit-Log\n\nEveryone. Who changed what: profile, team, API keys, webhooks, payout\ntargets and live access. Read-only, with no filter or export. Internal\nreview notes are not shown.\n\n### Integration\n\nOwners, admins and developers.\n\n- \"Four steps to your first test payment\": create a key, set the payout\n  target, create a payment, receive the result.\n- Three calls ready to copy: create a payment, check a webhook, check a\n  status. `CHAINMORE_API_KEY` and `CHAINMORE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` belong on the\n  server only.\n- \"Ask the ChainMore Concierge\" opens the chat.\n\n### Settings / Einstellungen\n\nOwners and admins.\n\n- \"Language\": the language of the dashboard.\n- \"Account overview\": account status, current mode, live access, and links\n  \"Manage keys\" and \"Manage webhooks\".\n- \"Merchant profile\": change the display name shown in the checkout, then\n  \"Save display name\". Result: \"Display name saved.\"\n- Legal name, default currency, account status and live access change only\n  through ChainMore: email `support@chainmore.io` with the merchant ID.\n- Password and sign-in: the dashboard has no password, two-factor or session\n  settings. For sign-in problems, email `support@chainmore.io`.\n\n### Top bar\n\n- Language: the EN/DE switch at the top. The choice is remembered in the\n  browser.\n- Light or dark: the moon or sun button at the top. Dark is the default.\n- User menu: shows the e-mail. \"Profile\" and \"Preferences\" both open\n  Settings, which only owners and admins can use.\n- Sign out: user menu, \"Sign out\", then \"Sign out now\". This also ends the\n  login; the next sign-in asks for the password again. There is no \"sign out\n  on all devices\".\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\nEach entry: what you see, what to check first, the steps, who can do them,\nwhat should happen, and when to stop and contact `support@chainmore.io`.\nRepeat an action only by hand and only after checking that it did not\nalready take effect.\n\n### The access e-mail link no longer works\n- Check: the newest access e-mail is used, and it is less than 72 hours old.\n- Steps: email `support@chainmore.io` from the registered address and ask for\n  a new access e-mail. There is no need to register again.\n- Who: the person the e-mail was for. ChainMore sends the new e-mail.\n- Result: a new e-mail with a working link.\n- Stop: if the new link fails too, tell support the time of the attempt and\n  what the page said.\n\n### \"The company terms still need to be accepted by an account owner or administrator.\"\n- Check: \"Your personal acknowledgements have been saved.\" is shown, so your\n  own part is done.\n- Steps: ask an owner or admin of the account to sign in and accept the\n  company terms. Then press \"Check saved status\" / \"Gespeicherten Status\n  prüfen\".\n- Who: an owner or admin. Nobody can accept on another person's behalf.\n- Result: \"Check saved status\" opens the dashboard.\n- Stop: if no owner or admin can sign in, email `support@chainmore.io`.\n\n### \"Your acknowledgement could not be confirmed. Check the saved status before trying again.\"\n- Check: press \"Check saved status\" first. If the dashboard opens, the save\n  went through.\n- Steps: if the page is still shown, save once more with the same choices.\n  Sending the same confirmation again is safe.\n- Who: the same person.\n- Result: the dashboard opens, or the page shows what is still missing.\n- Stop: if it fails again, email `support@chainmore.io` with the time.\n\n### \"Your account documents could not be checked\" or \"Your saved account status could not be checked\"\n- Meaning: ChainMore could not check the confirmations at that moment (code\n  `merchant_acceptance_unavailable`). The dashboard stays closed on purpose\n  until it can.\n- Steps: wait a minute, then press \"Check saved status\" or reload the page.\n- Who: anyone on the page.\n- Result: the dashboard opens, or the documents page shows what is missing.\n- Stop: if it stays, email `support@chainmore.io` with the time and the\n  e-mail address used to sign in.\n\n### The documents page appears again\n- Check: the \"Document version\" line. A new version needs new\n  confirmations; the company terms of the new version need an owner or admin\n  again.\n- Steps: read the documents shown and confirm them. If a save reports that\n  the documents changed (code `merchant_acceptance_document_changed`), reload\n  the page and confirm the version now shown.\n- Who: every person for themselves; an owner or admin for the company terms.\n- Result: the dashboard opens again.\n- Stop: questions about the content of the documents go to\n  `support@chainmore.io`.\n\n### Error code `merchant_acceptance_forbidden`\n- Meaning: the confirmation was refused for this sign-in, for example\n  because only an owner or admin can accept the company terms, or because\n  the membership is no longer active. Nothing was saved.\n- Steps: reload the dashboard and sign in again with your own account.\n- Who: company terms only an owner or admin; personal acknowledgements every\n  person for themselves.\n- Stop: if it stays, email `support@chainmore.io` with the time and the\n  e-mail address used to sign in.\n\n### Error code `merchant_first_login_required`\n- Meaning: the account documents still need confirming, by this person or by\n  an owner or admin for the company. Nothing was changed.\n- Steps: reload the dashboard. The documents page shows what is missing.\n- Who: as described in \"First sign-in\".\n\n### \"The mode changed. The request was not applied.\"\n- Meaning: the mode changed after the page was loaded, in another tab or on\n  ChainMore's side (codes `dashboard_mode_changed` or\n  `dashboard_context_changed`). The refused request changed nothing.\n- Check: the mode shown in the bar below the top bar.\n- Steps: if it is the mode you want, do the action again by hand, once.\n  Otherwise pick the mode with \"Dashboard mode\" / \"Dashboard-Modus\" first.\n  For keys, payout targets and webhooks, look at the current list before\n  repeating.\n- Who: the same person.\n- Result: the action applies in the mode shown.\n- Stop: if it keeps happening, close other dashboard tabs and press \"Refresh\n  mode\" / \"Modus aktualisieren\"; then email `support@chainmore.io` with the\n  Error ID.\n\n### Error code `dashboard_mode_required`\n- Meaning: the request did not say which mode the dashboard shows, so it was\n  refused. Nothing was changed. An old tab after a dashboard update can cause\n  this.\n- Steps: reload the page and try once more.\n- Stop: if it stays, email `support@chainmore.io` with the Error ID.\n\n### \"The mode could not be confirmed. Please refresh.\"\n- Steps: press \"Refresh mode\" / \"Modus aktualisieren\". If the message stays,\n  reload the page.\n- Stop: if it stays after a reload, email `support@chainmore.io`.\n\n### The registration was approved, but the dashboard shows test mode\n- Meaning: approval of the registration opens the account in test mode. Live\n  access is a separate step; see \"Test and live mode\".\n- Steps: when testing is complete, email `support@chainmore.io` to ask for\n  live access. Once it is on, pick \"Live mode\" / \"Live-Modus\" in the\n  selector.\n- Who: ChainMore switches live access on after reviewing the business\n  profile, which an owner or admin submits. Each person then picks their own\n  mode.\n\n### \"This page is not available for your role\" or \"Your role can't make this change\"\n- Meaning: the role of the signed-in person does not include this page or\n  action.\n- Steps: ask an owner or admin to do it, or to change your role on the Team\n  page.\n- Who: an owner or admin.\n- Stop: there is no way around a role; the Concierge cannot change roles.\n\n### \"No merchant account linked to your sign-in\"\n- Meaning: the sign-in worked, but this e-mail address is not a member of a\n  merchant account.\n- Steps: sign out and sign in with the address that was invited, or ask an\n  owner or admin to invite this address.\n- Who: an owner or admin sends invitations.\n\n### \"Your session expired.\" or \"We couldn't read your sign-in\"\n- Steps: sign in again. For \"We couldn't read your sign-in\", sign out first,\n  then sign in.\n- Stop: if sign-in keeps failing, email `support@chainmore.io`.\n\n### \"Something went wrong\" with an Error ID\n- Steps: when a page did not load, press \"Reload page\" once. After an action\n  (save, create, rotate, revoke), first check whether the change is visible,\n  then decide whether to do it again.\n- Stop: if it keeps failing, use \"Contact support\" or email\n  `support@chainmore.io` with the Error ID.\n\n### Messages from the ChainMore Concierge itself\n- \"The ChainMore Concierge opens once your merchant account is set up.\" can\n  also mean that the account documents still need confirming. Reload the\n  dashboard; if the documents page appears, complete it.\n- \"The ChainMore Concierge is not reachable right now.\": try again later, or\n  email `support@chainmore.io`.\n- \"Too many questions in a short time.\": wait a minute.\n- \"Your account reached today's limit for Concierge questions.\": try again\n  tomorrow, or email `support@chainmore.io`.\n\n## What the Concierge cannot do\n\nThe Concierge only explains. It cannot see or change the merchant's account,\npayments, keys, payout targets, team or settings, and it never asks for\npasswords, API keys or secrets.\n";
